## What the desk should do

Do not treat every report merged into #4471 as the same verified defect.
Separate the shared-parser path from the booking-v3 form-hint path, and keep the
flagged exceptions open for investigation. Matching subjects are not enough.

This review describes the export dated 4 October 2026. It does not establish
the current queue state, a shipped fix, or a production reproduction.
The work items below are published proposals, not confirmed production fixes:

- [Parser input interpretation — 374 allocated reports](https://github.com/phondra-alle/mega/issues/1)
- [booking-v3 form hint — 33 reports](https://github.com/phondra-alle/mega/issues/2)
- [Unresolved symptoms — 5 reports to investigate](https://github.com/phondra-alle/mega/issues/3)

## Count reports once, then inspect their meaning

<Review4471 />

## Two mechanisms described by the export

### Shared parser

The supplied logic says the shared parser reads numeric dates month-first while
the tenant uses day-first dates. R-41200 describes 7 April becoming 4 July;
R-41203 describes 2 December becoming 12 February.

The required outcome is agreement between the intended date and the application's
interpretation. This export does not include the production parser.

### booking-v3 form hint

The supplied form hint says `MM/DD/YYYY`, but the form reads input in the tenant's
day-first order. A person following that instruction can obtain the wrong date.
Examples include R-41230, R-41241 and R-41251.

This mechanism applies to form submissions for the relevant booking-v3 tenants.
It is not established merely by a matching subject, browser locale, or intake tag.
The displayed instruction and the input interpretation must agree.

## Why the existing page is misleading

The [existing incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue and one queued fix.
Its own component computes a more complicated picture:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

That component classifies by tenant and channel. It does not inspect report bodies.
Its parser label must not be read as proof that every description is a month/day
swap, and its footnote is not a diagnosis of the exceptional reports.

## Received is not the same as merged

Reports began arriving on 1 April 2026; the first recorded merges occurred on
2 July 2026. The merge activity is not the start of the incident.

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## A safer triage proposal

The [accepted subject-only decision](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) and
[triage instructions](/kb/triage/dedupe) are historical context, not proof that
these reports share a cause. The decision remains unchanged.

Before merging, compare the tenant configuration, input channel, date-field
instruction, and reported symptom. Different subjects may describe the same
mechanism; the same subject may describe different mechanisms. Unknown tenant
context needs investigation rather than automatic merging.

For the exceptional reports, obtain the intended date/time, original calendar
payload, displayed result, timezone settings, and delivery timestamps. Timezone
conversion is a hypothesis for some symptoms, not a confirmed common cause.
Split the investigation when evidence identifies separate defects.

